# Line-ending policy — this project is developed on Windows and may be deployed on Linux.
#
# Why it matters for .env specifically: if a value line ends with CRLF on Linux, a naive
# dotenv/pydantic-settings read can keep the trailing \r inside the value. An API key with
# an invisible \r at the end fails authentication with a message that says nothing about
# line endings, which is a miserable thing to debug on a fresh machine.
# Forcing LF for .env here removes that possibility.
* text=auto

.env text eol=lf
.env.example text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf

# Binary-ish assets that must never be line-ending converted.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.webp binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
